{
  "about": [
    "Kenyan people, institutions and places that spaCy's small English model does not know.",
    "Loaded by backend/nlp/entities.py into an EntityRuler that runs before spaCy's own entity model.",
    "people: one entry per person. 'id' identifies them; every alias must point to that person alone.",
    "names_without_identity: tagged as PERSON but never resolved to one person, because the corpus uses them for several:",
    "  'Odinga' is Raila, Winnie or Oburu; 'Nyoro' is Ndindi Nyoro and a former Kiambu governor; 'Lusaka' is also Zambia's capital, so it is left out entirely.",
    "case_sensitive: matched only as written, for names that are also ordinary words ('Jubilee', 'Wiper', 'Senate', and 'KURA', which is Swahili for 'vote').",
    "Apostrophes are matched straight, curly and dropped: Matiang'i, Matiang'i and Matiangi.",
    "Longest match wins, so 'Uhuru Park' is a place and 'Kenyatta University' an organisation, while 'Uhuru' alone is a person.",
    "Titles are deliberately not part of any name: 'Former DP Gachagua' matches 'Gachagua', and the title is read separately.",
    "Sources: titles and names as they appear in this corpus's own headlines and snippets (mined, then checked by hand). Add new names as they appear."
  ],
  "as_of": "2026-10",

